### State-integrity checks for CI

Keep an approved state digest outside the Pulumi backend and compare it before deployment:

```bash
set -euo pipefail

STACK="org/project/prod"
STATE_FILE="$(mktemp)"

pulumi stack export \
  --stack "$STACK" \
  --show-secrets=false \
  > "$STATE_FILE"

CURRENT_HASH="$(sha256sum "$STATE_FILE" | awk '{print $1}')"
EXPECTED_HASH="$(cat .security/approved-state.sha256)"

if [[ "$CURRENT_HASH" != "$EXPECTED_HASH" ]]; then
  echo "State integrity check failed."
  echo "Review the exported state and require security approval."
  exit 1
fi

pulumi preview --stack "$STACK" --diff --non-interactive
```

